monitor: MON or WOZ [line]  then:  addr  addr.addr  addr:b b b  addrR  X leaves
files:   DIR [A]  CD [dir]  MKDIR dir  RM name  RMDIR dir  TYPE name  XD name
         LOAD name [addr]  SAVE name from.to  RENAME old new  CP old new
         RUN [name.prg|addr]  EXEC script   (bare names search the language dirs)
         an unknown word runs name.prg from disk, with args (ARGS call $FF95)
         names starting with . are hidden from DIR (DIR A shows them)
memory:  FILL from.to value   COPY from.to dest
system:  INFO  TIME  MODE [0-2] [0|1]  COLOR fg [bg]  ECHO  CLS  HUSH  RESET
         DUMP [note|ON|OFF]
tongues: BBC (BBC BASIC on the Tube)   CPM (CP/M 2.2, the Z80 second processor)
         FORTH (Tali Forth 2, native)  EHBASIC via RUN EHBASIC
network: a URL is a file name (Meatloaf): TYPE http://host/file  CP http://host/x.prg x.prg
         RUN http://host/x.prg  LOAD "http://..." in EhBASIC and BBC BASIC
         CD tnfs://host/dir puts the current directory on a TNFS server (FujiNet,
         Meatloaf): DIR lists it, bare names load from it, CD .. climbs, CD - comes home
         TELNET host port (F12 hangs up) on the N: device at $D900; ANSI/VT100 via JIM
terminal: JIM at $DA00, a VT100/ANSI in hardware: CP/M programs and BBC BASIC draw
         through it (install CP/M programs for VT100 or ANSI); TELNET too
boot:    /!BOOT runs as an EXEC script at power-on; hold a key to skip it
